rsa-openssl.json contains independent signatures generated with OpenSSL 3.6.3.
Only the public key, input, and signatures are retained. The temporary test
private key was generated with:

  openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out key.pem
  openssl pkey -in key.pem -pubout

For each SHA-256, SHA-384, and SHA-512 digest, the corpus includes PKCS#1 v1.5
and PSS with exact salt lengths 0, 1, digest length, and maximum for RSA-2048.
Signatures were generated over the verbatim UTF-8 message field with:

  openssl dgst -sha256 -sign key.pem -out signature message
  openssl dgst -sha256 -sign key.pem -out signature \
    -sigopt rsa_padding_mode:pss -sigopt rsa_mgf1_md:sha256 \
    -sigopt rsa_pss_saltlen:0 message

The hash and salt options were varied for the remaining vectors. Tests verify
all signatures with the library helper and reject changed digests/parameters.
The deterministic zero-salt encoded messages are also compared directly to
the independent OpenSSL signature's recovered RSA representative. Separate
emulator tests verify library-generated signatures with Go crypto/rsa.
